# X2 -- Does a group Driver B draws behave as a DF wave? On a copy of the trial fort (saltwater river, tropical ocean): the water layer drawn by the tool, two groups at once, a 24 ceiling, a 1-2 day gap, a 9,000-tick countdown, coupling and cohesion on, every water species active all year. Per drawn group: it stays together (cohesion: a school), leaves on its countdown, debits the entry at the draw and is refunded as it leaves, lands in water that suits its body and salinity, and a prey draw calls its predators next.
